# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the test suite.
#
# OpenSSL keeps DRBG state in its secure heap, an mmap'd arena that
# LeakSanitizer does not scan. Once any secure allocation has initialised
# that heap, the per-thread DRBGs of the library context look unreachable
# even though they are owned by it. Nothing in this project allocates
# them, so hide every object reached through a DRBG instantiation.
leak:rand_new_drbg
